  "solution": {
    "text": "As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> will try to rotate the ring is clockwise direction friction will oppose the rotation and provide translational motion. so frictional force will act forward.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0013900_AnsExp1_1-.jpg\" /><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mn>d&#964; = (dq)</mn> <mo>&#215;</mo> <mn>(</mn> <msub> <mn>E</mn> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mn>)</mn> <mn>2R sin &#952;</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mn>d&#964; = (&#955; Rd&#952;) 2RE</mn> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mn>sin &#952;</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>&#964;</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msup> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mtext>&#955;</mtext> <msub> <mtext>E</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <munderover> <mo>&#8747;</mo> <mn>0</mn> <mrow> <mtext>&#960;</mtext> <mo>/</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </munderover> <mtext>sin&#160;</mtext> <mtext>&#952;</mtext> <mtext>d</mtext> <mtext>&#952;</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msup> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mtext>&#955;</mtext> <msub> <mtext>E</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mtext>...(1)</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />For translational motion,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br />For rotational motion ,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;...(3)<br /><br />From (2) and (3)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;...(4)<br /><br />From (1) and (4)<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#964;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#955;</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mi>f</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>r</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>",
